                  <section id="faqs" className="scroll-mt-32">
                    <h2 className="text-xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 md:mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                    <div className="space-y-4">
                      <div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm">
                        <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the primary benefit of drafting a contract for Lok Adalats?</h3>
                        <p className="text-gray-700">The primary benefit is speed. Traditional litigation in India takes years, whereas contracts specifically drafted with pre litigation mediation and Lok Adalat consent clauses can be resolved, and legally enforced, in an average of 45 days. This saves businesses immense amounts of capital and preserves the commercial relationships.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm">
                        <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can any commercial contract be resolved in a Lok Adalat?</h3>
                        <p className="text-gray-700">Most commercial, civil, and compoundable criminal disputes can be settled in a Lok Adalat, provided both parties agree to the settlement. Express consent clauses in the original contract make this process seamless by legally establishing the intent to conciliate prior to any dispute arising.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm">
                        <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a Lok Adalat award legally binding?</h3>
                        <p className="text-gray-700">Yes, an award passed by a Lok Adalat is considered equivalent to a decree of a civil court. It is final, binding on all parties, and no appeal lies against it in any standard court of law. This provides absolute legal certainty and immediate enforceability through execution proceedings.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm">
                        <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How does an ADR clause speed up the process?</h3>
                        <p className="text-gray-700">An Alternative Dispute Resolution clause mandates that parties must attempt mediation or conciliation before approaching a civil court. This legally compels participation in forums like Lok Adalats, preventing immediate, hostile litigation and forcing early dialogue.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm">
                        <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do we still need a lawyer if the case goes to Lok Adalat?</h3>
                        <p className="text-gray-700">While proceedings are simpler and non adversarial, having a specialized lawyer ensures your settlement terms are legally sound, protects your rights during negotiation, and handles the intricate procedural filings effectively with the District Legal Services Authority.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm">
                        <h3 className="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a previously drafted standard contract be taken to Lok Adalat?</h3>
                        <p className="text-gray-700">Yes, even standard contracts can be brought before a Lok Adalat at the pre litigation stage if both parties consent at that time. However, having specific Lok Adalat clauses pre drafted prevents one party from unilaterally delaying the process by refusing consent initially.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </section>


